  "notes": "Web 417 \u2014 UMAR-MIRROR-NO-DISPATCHES (Nov 11, 2026). A connected seat could not see the driver's UPCOMING dispatches at all. The field report: Asjad texted Umar (his Connect All seat) \"You still don't see my dispatches?\" \u2014 Umar: \"No nothing\" \u2014 while the Nov 11 Aecon Trans dispatch ran in progress. Investigation (tools/umar-mirror-no-dispatches-test.js, end to end over the real pipe + mirror): today's in-progress dispatch and yesterday's completed one already publish and render on the seat's Dispatch face on web 416 \u2014 the leg that was missing entirely is UPCOMING. (1) Publish: CP.publishRecent carries today + yesterday only, and the complete-history sweep runs once per NEW peer, so in a pair's steady state a future dispatch's day was never published until its own day arrived. New CP.publishUpcoming \u2014 every future date holding a dispatch record (list or active) \u2014 now rides every CP.publishAll cycle; publishDay's own gates (the work-profile fence, the nothing-to-share null) and its content guard still rule, so repeat cycles stay silent and a future date with no dispatch never writes. (2) Render: the mirror's Dispatch face fetched only (today-13 .. today); its window now reaches a week ahead, and future days render as an 'Upcoming dispatches' card of plain read-only rows above the last-14-days card, which is unchanged byte for byte (the v390 Limited tap-door stays on the past card only). Nothing else changed: the driver's own views, the multi-driver send screen, and Limited seats are untouched \u2014 a Limited peer gains only what her ticks already gave her (an unticked Limited seat is still blocked from the Dispatch face and the pipe reader still serves her none of his days). Bench: on pristine web 416 the new suite fails exactly the four upcoming assertions (no day doc for 2026-11-12; no Upcoming card); on 417 it passes 22/22 \u2014 today rides active/'Working now', yesterday rides completed with ticket 28830, tomorrow publishes as Scheduled and renders in the Upcoming card, the seat's OWN dispatch never appears under the driver's name, the face carries no action buttons, and a second publish cycle leaves the upcoming doc byte-identical. Verdict owed from Umar's phone via Asjad: his seat must show Asjad's dispatches \u2014 today's in progress and the next one booked.",
